.TH VECHO 1.SH NAMEvecho \- System V echo.SH SYNOPSIS\fBvecho\fR[argument ...].SH DESCRIPTION\fBvecho\fRwrites its arguments, separated by spaces, and a line end.  As System V'secho does, it leaves the line end off when the text ends in\fB\ec\fR:\fR\fBvecho one\fRwrites `one' and a carriage return,\fBvecho one\ec\fRwrites `one' and stops.  It came with less 1.77.